---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Biographie | Raphael Buchm&uuml;ller">
  <Header />

  <main class="page">
    <section class="about">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Biographie</p>
        <h1>Visual analytics, human-AI interaction, and applied data science.</h1>
        <p class="lead narrow">
          I am an academic researcher at TU Wien, where I am part of the CVAST lab and employed in the
          Bilateral AI Cluster. My research focuses on visual analytics and human-AI interaction, with
          interests in heterogeneous data, network analysis, geographical data science, the digital
          humanities, and explainable AI.
        </p>
        <p class="lead narrow">
          Before joining TU Wien, I was part of the DBVIS group at the University of Konstanz. My former
          industry and applied data science experience includes work with
          <a href="https://www.vidatics.de/">Vidatics GmbH</a>, work for
          <a href="https://www.spiegel.de/gesundheit/alkohol-trinken-sie-mehr-als-der-durchschnitt-a-699f900d-6ae0-4dc7-81fd-1b5885e900f0">DER SPIEGEL</a>,
          and active participation in
          <a href="https://correlaid.github.io/correlaidx-kn-education/">CorrelAid X Konstanz</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Teaching</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        I contributed to visualization, visual analytics, data mining, and applied data science teaching
        across several semesters.
      </p>
      <div class="teaching-list">
        <article>
          <span>Thesis supervision</span>
          <div>14+ successfully supervised bachelor and master theses</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Fall school</span>
          <div><a href="https://cl-fallschool-2024.github.io/">Computational Linguistics Fall School 2024</a></div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2025 Summer</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Basic Concepts</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2024/2025 Winter</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Advanced Topics</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2024 Summer</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Basic Concepts<br />Applied Visual Analytics</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2023/2024 Winter</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Advanced Topics</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2023 Summer</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Basic Concepts<br />Applied Visual Analytics</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2022/2023 Winter</span>
          <div>Data Mining Basic Concepts</div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2022 Summer</span>
          <div>Data Visualization Basic Concepts</div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Research Projects & Proposals</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        I have contributed to 5+ active research proposal, project writing, and execution processes,
        especially around visual analytics, explainable AI, and human-AI collaboration.
      </p>
      <p>
        Selected projects and proposals I contributed to include:
      </p>
      <div class="project-cards">
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://www.scikon.uni-konstanz.de/en/projects/cuepaq/">CUEPAQ</a></h3>
            <p>
              Visual analytics and linguistics project on capturing, understanding, and explaining
              personalized argument quality. My work connects argument data, projections, and
              interactive explanation for richer analysis of argumentative structures.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://www.bilateral-ai.net/home">Bilateral AI Cluster</a></h3>
            <p>
              FWF Cluster of Excellence combining symbolic and sub-symbolic AI toward broader,
              more explainable AI systems. My role is situated at the visual analytics interface:
              making AI behavior, data curation, and model explanations inspectable.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://www.sfbtrr161.de/">SFB-TRR 161</a></h3>
            <p>
              Collaborative research center on quantitative methods for visual computing, with
              research areas spanning models, measures, adaptive algorithms, interaction, and
              applications. This shaped my work on evaluating and explaining visual analytic methods.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://www.cvast.tuwien.ac.at/project/sinoisi">SINOISI</a></h3>
            <p>
              CVAST project context around visual analytics and sensemaking for complex information
              spaces. I connect this line of work to interactive exploration, human-AI collaboration,
              and explanation-centered interfaces.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Challenges & Community</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="project-cards compact-projects">
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://mozart.diei.unipg.it/gdcontest/">Graph Drawing Contest</a></h3>
            <p>
              I enjoy taking part in challenge formats because they sharpen problem framing,
              visual reasoning, and fast prototyping around graph and network visualization tasks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://ieeevis.org/attachments/vis18-program.pdf">VAST Challenge</a></h3>
            <p>
              VAST-style challenge settings are a useful testbed for sensemaking under uncertainty:
              complex data, suspicious-pattern analysis, and visual analytics workflows under time pressure.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div>
            <h3><a href="https://arcprize.org/competitions/2026">ARC-AGI Challenge</a></h3>
            <p>
              I am currently participating in the ARC-AGI challenge, exploring abstract reasoning,
              agentic interaction, and how systems can infer rules from sparse examples.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Supervisors</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="supervisor-list">
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.cvast.tuwien.ac.at/team/silvia-miksch">Silvia Miksch</a>
          <span>Head of CVAST and Professor for Visual Analytics at TU Wien.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://elisabethlex.info/">Elisabeth Lex</a>
          <span>Full Professor at Graz University of Technology, working on recommender systems, information retrieval, and data science.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.vis.uni-konstanz.de/en/members/keim/">Daniel A. Keim</a>
          <span>Professor of Computer Science and chairholder of the DBVIS group at the University of Konstanz.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
